{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XHiZNaX2QH7mAcdGTiVYLv","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Aurora Phase 2 â€” Execution Log\n2\t\n3\tForeman records per-wave build outcomes below. 8 wave(s) planned\n4\t(Wave 1-2 = security hardening H1-H2; Wave 3-8 = llm.py upgrades L1-L6).\n5\t\n6\t## Waves\n7\t\n8\t### Wave 1 â€” H1: Payload-depth security scan â€” GREEN (2026-06-06)\n9\t\n10\t- **Deliverable:** `bin/scan_payload_depth.py` â€” re-fetches each scannable artifact's\n11\t  payload (payloads not retained on disk; reuses `fetcher` 7-day cache) and runs the real\n12\t  `payload_extractor.extract â†’ detectors â†’ scorer.score` path, persisting via\n13\t  `gate.write_verdict` in enforce mode. Monotonic re-stamp guard delegates to\n14\t  `gate._worst_status` (worst-wins; never raises servability). `--limit/--dry-run/--audit-out`.\n15\t- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 799 passed (793 after EXECUTE, +6 after FIX; baseline 752).\n16\t  No test weakening. No new `security_status IN (...)` literal (single-owner test green).\n17\t- **Review:** 2 independent reviewers. R1 GO (no blocker). R2 GO with 2 MAJORs:\n18\t  F1 (non-GitHub zero-byte fetch falsely labeled `payload-depth`), F2 (errors didn't gate\n19\t  exit/coverage). FIX iter 1 closed both + 2 MINORs; closure VERIFIER mutation-tested each\n20\t  fix â†’ all CLOSED, invariants intact â†’ GO.\n21\t- **Honesty fix (F1):** only genuinely fetched-and-scanned artifacts get `scan_depth:\n22\t  payload-depth`; no-payload artifacts (â‰ˆ506/775, mostly arxiv) get `served-text-fallback`\n23\t  and keep their monotonic value (not newly quarantined). Coverage breakdown in the audit.\n24\t- **SEPARATELY-AUTHORIZED (not run):** the live re-stamp against kb/aurora.db. Build delivers\n25\t  the CLI + tests only.\n26\t\n27\t### Wave 2 â€” H2: Evidence-loop promotion machinery â€” GREEN (2026-06-06)\n28\t\n29\t- **Deliverables:** real per-iteration LLM `make_live_score_fn` in `roles/evidence.py`