is now priced so\n  an `AURORA_*_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8` override meters correctly instead of $0 (closes a $0-fiction\n  hole on the Opus override path) + a deprecated-Opus guard test. The tokenizer factor + estimate\n  helpers are correct, tested, forward-ready, but **inert until a token-budget pre-flight consumer\n  exists**. (F3, LOW: a future 4.7+ model added without the field silently estimates at 1.0.)\n\n### Wave 8 â€” L6: Message Batches API â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n\n- **Deliverables:** `llm.py` `submit_anthropic_batch` + poll/collect + `build_anthropic_request_params`\n  (params identical to the synchronous shape incl. L2 cache / L3 tools / L4 effort + budget_tokens\n  guard) + `_meter_batch_result` (records each result `batch_mode=True` â†’ L1's 0.5Ã— from real usage);\n  `roles/batch_sweep.py` opt-in coordinator (`AURORA_BATCH_SWEEP`, default off); critic_a/reconciler\n  refactored into `build_prompt`/`parse_verdict` + a `prefetched_text` param; orchestrator batches\n  critic_a behind the flag. Per-item failure / timeout / missing result â†’ synchronous degrade\n  (`batch_mode=False`, `_note_degrade`); missing security-judge result â†’ abstain (fail-closed).\n- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 915 passed (+17). No test weakening.\n- **Review:** 2 reviewers, both GO. Flag-off path verified byte-for-byte (git-diff-confirmed the\n  critic_a/reconciler parse extraction is verbatim; equivalence also guarded by existing\n  test_structured_outputs + test_critic_c); batch metered exactly 0.5Ã—; per-item degrade + ~65-min\n  poll-timeout-degrade + judge fail-closed all tested; budget_tokens guard runs on batch params.\n- **HONEST OUTCOME / TRIPWIRE:** like L2/L5, this is **ready plumbing, not a current win**. Only\n  critic_a is wired (1 of 3 per-candidate Anthropic calls, â‰¤400 tokens); reconciler-batch +\n  judge-batch are built+tested but unwired (reconciler has a hard data-dependency on critic output;\n  judge is on the separate gate path). At TOP_K=2 that's ~2 small calls/night â†’ sub-cent savings, and\n  the blocking poll (up to ~65 min) makes `AURORA_BATCH_SWEEP=1` **net-negative EV at current scale**.\n  Default-off is correct; revisit only if TOP_K rises substantially.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2 â€” PROJECT DONE â€” 2026-06-07\n\nAll 8 planned waves built EXECUTE â†’ ADVERSARIAL-REVIEW (2 independent reviewers) â†’ FIX â†’ RE-REVIEW\nand converged GREEN, in order, on branch `foreman/aurora-revamp`.\n\n- **Security thread (Wave 1-2, live verdict path):** H1 payload-depth scan (monotonic, honest\n  scan-depth labeling) + H2 evidence-loop promotion machinery (default-legacy, nightly zero-cost,\n  $0-shadowâ†’NO-GO gate, adoption monotonic-toward-stricter). Both real value.\n- **llm.py thread (Wave 3-8):** L1 cost substrate (real, enabling) Â· L3 structured outputs (real\n  robustness + safe degrade) Â· L4 budget_tokens guard + thinking fold (real â€” prevents Opus 4.8 400s,\n  guards the $118 class). **L2 caching / L5 retarget / L6 batch are correct, honest, forward-ready\n  PLUMBING that is largely INERT at Aurora's current prompt sizes + TOP_K=2** â€” exactly the research's\n  \"validate before banking\" caveat, now measured.\n- **Ground-truth gate:** `python -m pytest` = **915 passed** (+163 across the 8 waves from the 752\n  Phase-1 baseline). No test weakening anywhere; security suite green throughout.\n- **Locked-preserved intact:** KB schema + library, single-owner security gate, deterministic cost\n  telemetry (post-call metering never altered by any wave), Helping Hand + publisher.\n- **SEPARATELY-AUTHORIZED, NOT run:** H2 SA-1 (metered shadow batch) + SA-2 (live evidence-engine\n  flip); the live H1 payload re-stamp against kb/aurora.db. All gated, default-off.\n- **Commits:** 0eca5f2 (W1) Â· ffae677 (W2) Â· 2618f59 (W3) Â· 0a24914 (W4) Â· f046810 (W5) Â· e604fa4\n  (W6) Â· 7b23c9e (W7) Â· + W8. Not pushed; awaiting John's review.\n","numLines":189,"startLine":1,"totalLines":189}}}
