egacy 4-arg path byte-for-byte unchanged); L3 structured outputs (forced `emit_result` tool-use + fail-closed/safe-degrade to plain text); L4 `effort`/adaptive-thinking with a recursive `_assert_no_budget_tokens` guard (prevents Opus 4.8 400s) + thinking-token fold (guards the \"$118 lesson\").\n- **Honest no-ops / forward-ready plumbing:** **L2 prompt caching** is a no-op at current prompt sizes (stable prefixes 15â€“60Ã— below model minimums; gated, activates only if a prefix ever exceeds the minimum); **L5 retarget** â€” estimate helpers are dead code (Aurora budgets in fixed-USD, not token pre-flight), its only concrete win is pricing `claude-opus-4-8` so an Opus override meters correctly instead of $0; **L6 Message Batches** is built/tested but only critic_a is wired (â‰¤400 tok), and the ~65-min blocking poll makes `AURORA_BATCH_SWEEP=1` net-negative EV at TOP_K=2.\n- These three explicitly confirm the AuroraTwo research's \"validate before banking\" caveat â€” now measured as largely inapplicable at current scale.\n\n**Preserved & deferred**\n- Locked invariants intact: KB schema + library, single-owner security gate, deterministic post-call cost metering (never altered by any wave), Helping Hand + publisher.\n- **SEPARATELY-AUTHORIZED, not run:** H2 SA-1 (metered shadow batch â‰¥200) + SA-2 (live evidence-engine flip); the live H1 payload re-stamp against `kb/aurora.db`. All gated, default-off.\n- Commits 0eca5f2 (W1) Â· ffae677 (W2) Â· 2618f59 (W3) Â· 0a24914 (W4) Â· f046810 (W5) Â· e604fa4 (W6) Â· 7b23c9e (W7) Â· + W8 â€” **not pushed; awaiting John's review.**\n\nOne note: the prompt's \"Anchors from the member documents\" section was empty, so I summarized against the full documents rather than specific anchor lines. If you meant particular anchors (specific waves or sections), point me at them and I'll tighten the summary to those."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7764